 is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}, "type": "feedback"}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Algorithm in Programming", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when talking about programming algorithms", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Identify information about algorithms related to software programming in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands key information in simple written and spoken texts about topics related to software programming and its history. Recognizes basic ideas on programming concepts and programming history in both written and spoken passages.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Simple Present Tense with Verb to Be Negative in Statements", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The verb <strong>to be</strong> is one of the most important verbs in English, and it can also be the easiest to learn.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<p>You use the verb <strong>to be</strong> to express the general status and characteristics of a person, an animal or an object.</p> <p>You use the verb <strong>to be</strong> in <strong>negative</strong> form to say that something is not a general state or is not true at the moment of speaking.</p> <p>Let&rsquo;s see the next structure:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Subject + verb to be + not + compliment.</p> <p>Example:</p> <ul> <li><i>Programming algorithms <strong>are</strong> <strong>not</strong> a computer code.</i></li> </ul> <p>You can also use contractions to express a <strong>negative</strong> sentence. Take a look at the following chart to have a better understanding of this topic: <i>&nbsp;</i></p>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb to Be Contraction with The Subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb to Be Contraction with The \\\"Not\\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I'm not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I'm not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You're not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You aren't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He's not/ she's not/ it's not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He isn't/ she isn't/ it isn't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We're not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We aren't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They're not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They aren't\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "But believe me when I say programming algorithms are not difficult", "type": "example"}, {"content": "All the steps have to be very clear; there is not space for interpretation when writing algorithms.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Algorithm Flowchart", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can write <strong>programming algorithms</strong> in two ways, as a numbered list or as a flowchart.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Using a<b> flowchart</b> to write a <u>programming algorithm</u> is very simple. All you have to do is to organize the steps of what you are going to do, as a recipe. The only difference of using a <b>flowchart</b> is that we need to use shapes (rectangles, parallelograms, and diamonds, among others) that represent specific actions and arrows to connect the steps among them.</br></br>  Let's imagine we are going to create a password for our email account. </br></br>  As a list it would look like this: </br></br> <ol> <li>Start. </br> <li>Create a variable to receive the user's password. </br> <li>Clear the variable in case it is not empty. </br> <li>Ask the user for a password. </br> <li>Store the response in the variable. </br> <li>Check if the stored response is a valid password. </br> <li>Not valid? Go back to step 3. </br> <li>End. </br></br>  This same exercise as a flowchart look like this:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob04img01.jpg", "type": "image"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "procedure ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a particular way to do something following precise steps", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A programming algorithm is the same, but the procedure is described by using programming language, which is the one the computer can understand. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "recipe ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a set of instructions to prepare something, especially food", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's imagine you are cooking using the help of a recipe. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "expected ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "likely or probable to happen or arrive", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Then, when the computer does the procedure, an outcome is expected; the outcome is the final result of the procedure.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "parallelogram", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a quadrilateral whose opposite sides are parallel and equal in length", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We also have the Data Object or I/O shape, a parallelogram which shows the inputs and outputs from a process; for the email password it contains the words Old password, New password, and Verify password. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "arrow", "type": "name"}, {"content": "line with a wedge-shaped end that shows the direction of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Finally, there is the Decision/Conditional Object, which is represented as a diamond with a question or statement in it and two arrows coming out of it representing its two possible answers, yes or no.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "shapes ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an external specific outline or figure ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In this case, when writing the algorithm you need the same steps just that you use shapes and arrows, creating a map route to the desired result.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Look for information about more programming algorithm samples. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write notes and select one of them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Design a poster to describe it, use visual aids.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share with your partners and solve questions.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I look for information about more programming algorithm samples. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe a programming algorithm sample.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about programming algorithm and its features.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}]}